      "claim": "In a DFS of a connected undirected graph, any edge not in the DFS tree connects a vertex to one of its ancestors (a back edge).",
      "evidence": "When DFS examines an edge (x,y) and y is already visited, y must be on the recursion stack, i.e., an ancestor of x; undirected graphs have no cross or forward edges.",
