      "id": 2,
      "claim": "For a non‑tree edge (u,v) with pre(u) < pre(v), u is an ancestor of v in the DFS tree.",
      "evidence": "From step 1 the edge joins an ancestor–descendant pair; preorder numbers increase when moving from ancestor to descendant, so the smaller preorder belongs to the ancestor.",
      "weight": 0.30,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "If u is an ancestor of v, then the lowest common ancestor of u and v is u.",
      "evidence": "The LCA is the deepest node that is ancestor of both; u itself is a common ancestor and any deeper common ancestor would have to be a descendant of u, which cannot be ancestor of u.",
      "weight": 0.15,
      "depends_on": [2]
    },
