      "id": 4,
      "claim": "In a postorder traversal, a descendant is visited before its ancestor, so post(v) < post(u) when u is ancestor of v.",
      "evidence": "Postorder records a node after all nodes in its subtree have been recorded; v lies in u’s subtree.",
